{
  "text": " I look up at my wooden ceiling and I think of how well I'm doing. I'm surrounded by warmth and beauty and I fit in. I let go of my past, I'm right here. I might take a walk on the beach later, if it's not too windy. I'll breathe in the sea air, I'll put on something that makes me feel good. There is nothing wrong with what you're wearing now. I am emotionally independent. I am the source of love. I generate my own happiness. I used to have a dog. I miss Doogie and my cat. I am in control of my thoughts. I decide which ones I'd like to keep and which ones to let go of. I'm happy to be me. If it wasn't me, I'd still like him and wish I could spend all my time with him. I like to show myself, appreciation that I deserve. I've got a box in my convertible. Maybe I'll take it for a spin later. There is nothing wrong with me. Thank you for watching!",
